el="Remove b2"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="add-indicator"><div class="row2"><input class="input" placeholder="Add an indicator by name" aria-label="Indicator name" maxlength="64" value=""><button class="btn" disabled="">Add</button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Hexagon (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Delta": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Delta"></div><div class="field"><label>Construct type</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Latent variable: indicators reflect the construct (ellipse)">Common factor</button><button class="" title="Emergent variable: a weighted combination of its indicators (hexagon)">Composite</button></div></div><div class="field"><label title="How this construct's indicator weights are estimated (each construct has its own mode)">Outer weights (this construct)</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Mode A (correlation)</button><button class="">Mode B (regression)</button><button class="" title="Equal weights on the standardised indicators (unit weights)">Sum scores</button><button class="" title="Weights you give, not estimated; rescaled so that the score has unit variance. Runs in the built-in engine">Pre-defined</button></div></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" checked=""><span><b>Categorical</b><br><span class="hint">d1’s k categories become k − 1 dummy variables (the first category is the reference) forming a composite (Mode B): the effect of group membership (Henseler 2021). Exogenous only.</span></span></label><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (1)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">d1</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove d1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="add-indicator"><div class="row2"><input class="input" placeholder="Add an indicator by name" aria-label="Indicator name" maxlength="64" value=""><button class="btn" disabled="">Add</button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Oval or circle (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Epsilon": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Epsilon"></div><div class="field"><label>Construct type</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Latent variable: indicators reflect the construct (ellipse)">Common factor</button><button class="" title="Emergent variable: a weighted combination of its indicators (hexagon)">Composite</button></div></div><div class="field"><label title="How this construct's indicator weights are estimated (each construct has its own mode)">Outer weights (this construct)</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Mode A (correlation)</button><button class="">Mode B (regression)</button><button class="" title="Equal weights on the standardised indicators (unit weights)">Sum scores</button><button class="" title="Weights you give, not estimated; rescaled so that the score has unit variance. Runs in the built-in engine">Pre-defined</button></div></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Categorical</b><br><span class="hint">e1’s k categories become k − 1 dummy variables (the first category is the reference) forming a composite (Mode B): the effect of group membership (Henseler 2021). Exogenous only.</span></span></label><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (1)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">e1</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove e1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Gamma": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Gamma"></div><div class="field"><label>Construct type</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Latent variable: indicators reflect the construct (ellipse)">Common factor</button><button class="" title="Emergent variable: a weighted combination of its indicators (hexagon)">Composite</button></div></div><div class="field"><label title="How this construct's indicator weights are estimated (each construct has its own mode)">Outer weights (this construct)</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Mode A (correlation)</button><button class="">Mode B (regression)</button><button class="" title="Equal weights on the standardised indicators (unit weights)">Sum scores</button><button class="" title="Weights you give, not estimated; rescaled so that the score has unit variance. Runs in the built-in engine">Pre-defined</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Second-order construct</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Measured by first-order constructs (two-stage approach): their scores are its indicators in stage 2. seminr weights it as chosen under Weighting. The components stay out of the structural model; connect this construct instead.</div><label class="check" style="margin-bottom: 4px;"><input type="checkbox" checked="">Alpha</label><label class="check" style="margin-bottom: 4px;"><input type="checkbox" checked="">Beta</label><label class="check" style="margin-bottom: 4px;"><input type="checkbox">Delta</label><label class="check" style="margin-bottom: 4px;"><input type="checkbox">Epsilon</label><label class="check" style="margin-bottom: 4px;"><input type="checkbox">Lambda</label></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Components (2)</div><div class="ind" style="align-items: center;"><span>Alpha</span></div><div class="ind" style="align-items: center;"><span>Beta</span></div><div class="ind-list"></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Oval or circle (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Lambda": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Lambda"></div><div class="field"><label>Construct type</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Latent variable: indicators reflect the construct (ellipse)">Common factor</button><button class="" title="Emergent variable: a weighted combination of its indicators (hexagon)">Composite</button></div></div><div class="field"><label title="How this construct's indicator weights are estimated (each construct has its own mode)">Outer weights (this construct)</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Mode A (correlation)</button><button class="">Mode B (regression)</button><button class="" title="Equal weights on the standardised indicators (unit weights)">Sum scores</button><button class="" title="Weights you give, not estimated; rescaled so that the score has unit variance. Runs in the built-in engine">Pre-defined</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Dominant indicator</label><select class="select"><option value="">None (sign as estimated)</option><option value="a1">a1</option><option value="a2">a2</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 4px;">Fixes the construct’s sign: its scores point the way this indicator does (loading positive), in the estimate and every bootstrap draw. cSEM and the built-in engine.</div></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (2)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">a1</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove a1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div><div class="ind"><span class="vname">a2</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove a2"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="add-indicator"><div class="row2"><input class="input" placeholder="Add an indicator by name" aria-label="Indicator name" maxlength="64" value=""><button class="btn" disabled="">Add</button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Oval or circle (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
}
`;

exports[`Inspector markup > every construct, process 1`] = `
{
  "Alpha": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Alpha"></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Conditional process analysis</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Scale score: the mean of its 3 items (computed per case before the regressions).</div><div class="field"><label>Scale</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Mean of the items, then OLS regression (as PROCESS)">Mean score</button><button class="" title="Latent variable: structural-after-measurement estimation (lavaan::sam), free of the attenuation that measurement error causes in mean scores. Confidence intervals by Monte Carlo.">Latent variable</button></div></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Covariate</b><br><span class="hint">Enters every equation (mediators and outcome) as a control variable, as PROCESS’s cov option. A covariate has no paths of its own.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (3)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">a1</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove a1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div><div class="ind"><span class="vname">a2</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove a2"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div><div class="ind"><span class="vname">a3</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove a3"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="add-indicator"><div class="row2"><input class="input" placeholder="Add an indicator by name" aria-label="Indicator name" maxlength="64" value=""><button class="btn" disabled="">Add</button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Oval or circle (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Beta": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Beta"></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Conditional process analysis</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Scale score: the mean of its 2 items (computed per case before the regressions).</div><div class="field"><label>Scale</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Mean of the items, then OLS regression (as PROCESS)">Mean score</button><button class="" title="Latent variable: structural-after-measurement estimation (lavaan::sam), free of the attenuation that measurement error causes in mean scores. Confidence intervals by Monte Carlo.">Latent variable</button></div></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Covariate</b><br><span class="hint">Enters every equation (mediators and outcome) as a control variable, as PROCESS’s cov option. A covariate has no paths of its own.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (2)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">b1</span><span class="num muted" title="Weight"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove b1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div><div class="ind"><span class="vname">b2</span><span class="num muted" title="Weight"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove b2"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="add-indicator"><div class="row2"><input class="input" placeholder="Add an indicator by name" aria-label="Indicator name" maxlength="64" value=""><button class="btn" disabled="">Add</button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Hexagon (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Delta": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Delta"></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Conditional process analysis</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Observed variable d1.</div><div class="field"><label>Measurement level</label><select class="select"><option value="">Continuous (or dichotomous)</option><option value="indicator">Categorical X: indicator coding</option><option value="sequential">Categorical X: sequential coding</option><option value="helmert">Categorical X: Helmert coding</option><option value="effect">Categorical X: effect coding</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">X with k groups becomes k − 1 codes; every effect of X is reported per code as a relative effect (Hayes &amp; Preacher, 2014), with the codes as PROCESS’s mcx option.</div></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Covariate</b><br><span class="hint">Enters every equation (mediators and outcome) as a control variable, as PROCESS’s cov option. A covariate has no paths of its own.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (1)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">d1</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove d1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="add-indicator"><div class="row2"><input class="input" placeholder="Add an indicator by name" aria-label="Indicator name" maxlength="64" value=""><button class="btn" disabled="">Add</button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Oval or circle (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Epsilon": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Epsilon"></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Conditional process analysis</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Observed variable e1.</div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" checked=""><span><b>Covariate</b><br><span class="hint">Enters every equation (mediators and outcome) as a control variable, as PROCESS’s cov option. A covariate has no paths of its own.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (1)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">e1</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove e1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Gamma": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Gamma"></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Conditional process analysis</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Drop a data column on this variable, or several items of a scale.</div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Covariate</b><br><span class="hint">Enters every equation (mediators and outcome) as a control variable, as PROCESS’s cov option. A covariate has no paths of its own.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Components (2)</div><div class="ind" style="align-items: center;"><span>Alpha</span></div><div class="ind" style="align-items: center;"><span>Beta</span></div><div class="ind-list"></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Oval or circle (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
  "Lambda": "<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Construct</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Name</label><input class="input" maxlength="100" value="Lambda"></div><div class="field"><label>Indicator side</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on" title="Indicators on the left" aria-label="Indicators on the left" aria-pressed="true"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M3 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the top" aria-label="Indicators on the top" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 3h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the right" aria-label="Indicators on the right" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M21 6v12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button><button class="" title="Indicators on the bottom" aria-label="Indicators on the bottom" aria-pressed="false"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="10" height="10" rx="2.5"></rect><path d="M6 21h12" stroke-width="3"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Conditional process analysis</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Latent variable measured by its 2 items, corrected for measurement error.</div><div class="field"><label>Scale</label><div class="segmented"><button class="" title="Mean of the items, then OLS regression (as PROCESS)">Mean score</button><button class="on" title="Latent variable: structural-after-measurement estimation (lavaan::sam), free of the attenuation that measurement error causes in mean scores. Confidence intervals by Monte Carlo.">Latent variable</button></div></div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Covariate</b><br><span class="hint">Enters every equation (mediators and outcome) as a control variable, as PROCESS’s cov option. A covariate has no paths of its own.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Indicators (2)</div><div class="ind-list"><div class="ind"><span class="vname">a1</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove a1"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div><div class="ind"><span class="vname">a2</span><span class="num muted" title="Loading"></span><button class="btn icon ghost sm" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;" aria-label="Remove a2"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="add-indicator"><div class="row2"><input class="input" placeholder="Add an indicator by name" aria-label="Indicator name" maxlength="64" value=""><button class="btn" disabled="">Add</button></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Drawn as</label><div class="row2"><select class="select" aria-label="Shape"><option value="">Oval or circle (its type)</option><option value="rectangle">Rectangle</option><option value="octagon">Octagon</option></select><span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"><input aria-label="Colour" type="color" value="#ffffff"></span></div></div><button class="btn danger"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M10 11v6M14 11v6"></path><path d="M6 7l1 12a2 2 0 002 2h6a2 2 0 002-2l1-12M9 7V4h6v3"></path></svg> Delete construct</button></div></div></aside>",
}
`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, cbsem 1`] = `
"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" is a composite: in CB-SEM composites cannot be higher-order constructs or their components.</span></div><div class="issue warning clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" has two indicators; it is only identified through its relations with other factors.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" has pre-defined weights, a PLS-SEM option: switch to PLS-SEM, or estimate its weights.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>No correlation is drawn between Gamma ↔ Lambda: as exogenous constructs they are estimated as uncorrelated. Intended?</span><span class="issue-actions"><button class="btn sm">Correlate them</button><button class="btn sm ghost">Keep uncorrelated</button></span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>a3 is ordinal: choose the WLSMV estimator (thresholds and polychoric correlations), or treat it as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Mean replacement would put non-category values into ordinal indicators; choose casewise deletion.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Delta is marked categorical, which PLS-SEM and CPA use; CB-SEM treats it as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Alpha and Epsilon are fixed as uncorrelated, which applies to two exogenous constructs only. Delete the fixed zero.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Groups</div><select class="select"><option value="">One group (no grouping)</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">A grouping column is a numeric column with 2 to 20 values that is not an indicator (e.g. 1 = control, 2 = treatment).</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Clusters (two-level)</div><select class="select"><option value="">No clustering (one level)</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling weights</div><select class="select"><option value="">No weights</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling clusters</div><select class="select" aria-label="Sampling clusters"><option value="">No clustering</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">For cases sampled in clusters (schools, firms, countries) without modelling the levels: cluster-robust standard errors, as Mplus’s TYPE = COMPLEX.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Labels, defined parameters, tests</div><div class="hint">Right-click a path, loading or covariance → Label… Parameters with the same label are equal; labels can be used below.</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label>Held and labelled variances, intercepts, thresholds</label><div class="hint">Right-click a construct, its disturbance or an indicator → Variance…, Error variance…, Intercept… or a threshold, to hold one at a value, label it, or give values per group.</div></div><div class="field"><label>Defined parameters</label><button class="btn sm">Add defined parameter</button><div class="hint">Functions of labelled parameters, e.g. an indirect effect a*b or a difference a - b, with delta-method standard errors (lavaan :=).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Wald tests</label><button class="btn sm">Add Wald test</button><div class="hint">One hypothesis per line (left == right); all lines are tested jointly (lavaan::lavTestWald).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Constraints</label><textarea class="input mono" placeholder="a > 0
a < b
rel1 == rel2" spellcheck="false" rows="2"></textarea><div class="hint">One per line (left &gt; right, left &lt; right, or left == right), on labels and defined parameters; lavaan estimates under them. A parameter on its bound has no standard error, and χ² tests that involve active bounds are not standard.</div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>Keep variances non-negative<br><span class="hint">Bounds every variance at 0 (lavaan bounds = “pos.var”): instead of a negative variance (a Heywood case) the estimate stays at 0. Consider why it would be negative first: a misspecified model or too few cases.</span></span></label></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Covariances fixed at zero</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Not drawn: in a path diagram, no arrow means zero. Exogenous constructs otherwise covary freely.</div><div class="ind"><span>Alpha ↔ Epsilon</span><span></span><button class="btn sm ghost always" title="Let them covary freely again">Free</button></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="">PLS-SEM</button><button class="on">CB-SEM</button><button class="">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Covariance-based SEM. Common factors only; first loading of each factor fixed to 1.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Calculation engine"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">R packages</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Built-in</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">lavaan (Rosseel), running in your browser (webR), including bootstrapping (bootstrapLavaan). The first calculation loads the packages; your data never leave this computer. Monte Carlo simulation also runs in R (lavaan::simulateData, cSEM, lavaan).</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="r-backend">R runs in</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="r-backend"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on" title="webR: R compiled for the browser, with pinned package versions. Nothing to install.">This browser</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Desktop R on this computer, through the PLS Studio helper: native speed, all packages. Your data stay on this computer.">Desktop R (helper)</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">webR in this tab: nothing to install. For native speed (all cores, desktop R), get the PLS Studio Helper and choose Desktop R.<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-top: 6px;"><span class="helper-downloads"><a class="btn sm primary" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-arm64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Apple Silicon)</a><a class="btn sm" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-amd64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Intel)</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Other systems</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/blob/main/helper/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guide</a></span></div></div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="parallel-workers">Parallel bootstrap and simulation</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="parallel-workers" aria-disabled="false"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Off</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">2 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">4 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">6 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">8 sessions</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">One R session: bootstrap results are exactly those of a single run of the package with your seed. Applies to cSEM and lavaan bootstraps and Monte Carlo simulation in this browser; remembered here.</div></div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this model (data embedded): exactly what the R engine runs. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Latent interactions</div><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Product indicators</button><button class="">LMS</button><button class="">QML</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Products of mean-centred indicators (Marsh, Wen &amp; Hau, 2004), estimated by lavaan with the usual fit statistics.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Estimator</div><select class="select"><option value="ML">ML — maximum likelihood</option><option value="MLM">MLM — robust, Satorra–Bentler</option><option value="MLMV">MLMV — robust, mean- and variance-adjusted</option><option value="MLR">MLR — robust, Huber–White / Yuan–Bentler</option><option value="WLS">WLS — distribution-free (ADF / AGLS)</option><option value="GLS">GLS — generalised least squares</option><option value="WLSMV">WLSMV — robust weighted least squares (ordinal)</option><option value="RML">RML — robust ML, case-weighted (rsem)</option><option value="ULS">ULS — unweighted least squares</option><option value="2SLS">2SLS — MIIV two-stage least squares</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Normal-theory ML with expected-information standard errors.</div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox" checked=""><span>Standard errors from the observed information<br><span class="hint">The second derivatives of the log-likelihood at the estimates (lavaan information = “observed”; the default of Mplus for ML) instead of lavaan’s expected information. Estimates and χ² are the same; standard errors differ slightly.</span></span></label><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label for="cb-parameterization">Ordinal indicators: parameterisation</label><select id="cb-parameterization" class="select"><option value="delta">Delta (default): scale factors</option><option value="theta">Theta: residual variances</option></select><div class="hint">How the latent response behind each ordinal indicator is scaled. Delta fixes its total variance at 1; theta fixes its residual variance at 1, so residual variances can be held or freed (right-click an indicator), as in Mplus PARAMETERIZATION = THETA. The fit is the same; the scale of the estimates differs.</div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label for="cb-convention">Sample size in χ²</label><select id="cb-convention" class="select"><option value="lavaan">N (lavaan, Mplus)</option><option value="wishart">N − 1, Wishart likelihood (LISREL, EQS, Amos, the sem package)</option></select><div class="hint">Programs differ in whether χ² uses N or N − 1 and whether a covariance matrix is rescaled to its maximum-likelihood version; choose the convention of the program whose results you reproduce. Estimates of coefficients and loadings are the same; χ² and variances differ by a factor near N / (N − 1).</div></div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>CFI and TLI against uncorrelated variables<br><span class="hint">The baseline model in which every variable is uncorrelated (LISREL’s; lavaan’s when the syntax writes the covariances of exogenous variables out). By default the covariances among exogenous observed variables stay free in the baseline, as in Mplus and lavaan with fixed.x. Only matters with two or more exogenous observed variables.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Missing values</label><select class="select" aria-label="Missing values"><option value="mean">Mean replacement</option><option value="casewise">Casewise (listwise) deletion</option><option value="fiml">FIML (full-information maximum likelihood)</option><option value="twostage">Two-stage (Savalei &amp; Bentler)</option><option value="robusttwostage">Robust two-stage</option><option value="pairwise">Pairwise deletion</option><option value="mi">Multiple imputation</option></select></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Two-tailed</button><button class="" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Percentile</button><button class="" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button></div></div><div class="hint">Percentile intervals; p-values from two-tailed t tests. CB-SEM bootstraps standardised paths and indirect effects.</div></div></div></aside>"
`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, cbsem 2sls 1`] = `
"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Alpha": known reliabilities are not available with MIIV-2SLS; choose a maximum-likelihood estimator.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" is a composite: not available with MIIV-2SLS; choose a maximum-likelihood estimator.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Delta": a known reliability is not available with MIIV-2SLS; choose a maximum-likelihood estimator.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": MIIV-2SLS scales each factor by its first component; keep that loading at 1.</span></div><div class="issue warning clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" has two indicators; it is only identified through its relations with other factors.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" has pre-defined weights, a PLS-SEM option: switch to PLS-SEM, or estimate its weights.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Moderation (Beta moderating Alpha → Delta) is not available with MIIV-2SLS; choose a maximum-likelihood estimator.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>a3 is ordinal: choose the WLSMV estimator (thresholds and polychoric correlations), or treat it as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Mean replacement would put non-category values into ordinal indicators; choose casewise deletion.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>MIIV-2SLS has its own standard errors: the observed-information option is for the maximum-likelihood estimators.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Delta is marked categorical, which PLS-SEM and CPA use; CB-SEM treats it as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>QML is a maximum-likelihood method: choose the ML estimator.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>QML needs raw data and a single-group model without ESEM blocks or ordinal indicators.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Alpha and Epsilon are fixed as uncorrelated, which applies to two exogenous constructs only. Delete the fixed zero.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Groups</div><select class="select"><option value="">One group (no grouping)</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">A grouping column is a numeric column with 2 to 20 values that is not an indicator (e.g. 1 = control, 2 = treatment).</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Clusters (two-level)</div><select class="select"><option value="">No clustering (one level)</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling weights</div><select class="select"><option value="">No weights</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling clusters</div><select class="select" aria-label="Sampling clusters"><option value="">No clustering</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">For cases sampled in clusters (schools, firms, countries) without modelling the levels: cluster-robust standard errors, as Mplus’s TYPE = COMPLEX.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Labels, defined parameters, tests</div><div class="hint">Right-click a path, loading or covariance → Label… Parameters with the same label are equal; labels can be used below.</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label>Held and labelled variances, intercepts, thresholds</label><div class="hint">Right-click a construct, its disturbance or an indicator → Variance…, Error variance…, Intercept… or a threshold, to hold one at a value, label it, or give values per group.</div></div><div class="field"><label>Defined parameters</label><button class="btn sm">Add defined parameter</button><div class="hint">Functions of labelled parameters, e.g. an indirect effect a*b or a difference a - b, with delta-method standard errors (lavaan :=).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Wald tests</label><button class="btn sm">Add Wald test</button><div class="hint">One hypothesis per line (left == right); all lines are tested jointly (lavaan::lavTestWald).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Constraints</label><textarea class="input mono" placeholder="a > 0
a < b
rel1 == rel2" spellcheck="false" rows="2"></textarea><div class="hint">One per line (left &gt; right, left &lt; right, or left == right), on labels and defined parameters; lavaan estimates under them. A parameter on its bound has no standard error, and χ² tests that involve active bounds are not standard.</div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>Keep variances non-negative<br><span class="hint">Bounds every variance at 0 (lavaan bounds = “pos.var”): instead of a negative variance (a Heywood case) the estimate stays at 0. Consider why it would be negative first: a misspecified model or too few cases.</span></span></label></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Covariances fixed at zero</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Not drawn: in a path diagram, no arrow means zero. Exogenous constructs otherwise covary freely.</div><div class="ind"><span>Alpha ↔ Epsilon</span><span></span><button class="btn sm ghost always" title="Let them covary freely again">Free</button></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="">PLS-SEM</button><button class="on">CB-SEM</button><button class="">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Covariance-based SEM. Common factors only; first loading of each factor fixed to 1.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Calculation engine"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">R packages</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Built-in</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">MIIVsem (Fisher, Bollen, Gates &amp; Rönkkö), running in your browser (webR). The first calculation loads the packages; your data never leave this computer. Monte Carlo simulation also runs in R (lavaan::simulateData, cSEM, lavaan).</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="r-backend">R runs in</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="r-backend"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on" title="webR: R compiled for the browser, with pinned package versions. Nothing to install.">This browser</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Desktop R on this computer, through the PLS Studio helper: native speed, all packages. Your data stay on this computer.">Desktop R (helper)</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">webR in this tab: nothing to install. For native speed (all cores, desktop R), get the PLS Studio Helper and choose Desktop R.<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-top: 6px;"><span class="helper-downloads"><a class="btn sm primary" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-arm64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Apple Silicon)</a><a class="btn sm" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-amd64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Intel)</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Other systems</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/blob/main/helper/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guide</a></span></div></div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="parallel-workers">Parallel bootstrap and simulation</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="parallel-workers" aria-disabled="false"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Off</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">2 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">4 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">6 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">8 sessions</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">One R session: bootstrap results are exactly those of a single run of the package with your seed. Applies to cSEM and lavaan bootstraps and Monte Carlo simulation in this browser; remembered here.</div></div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this model (data embedded): exactly what the R engine runs. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Latent interactions</div><div class="segmented"><button class="">Product indicators</button><button class="">LMS</button><button class="on">QML</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Quasi-maximum likelihood (Klein &amp; Muthén, 2007; modsem): close to LMS, more robust to non-normal indicators. Fit statistics are for the model without the interaction. Bootstrap: cases are resampled and the model refitted with modsem, which is slow (LMS: seconds per sample); try 200 samples first.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Estimator</div><select class="select"><option value="ML">ML — maximum likelihood</option><option value="MLM">MLM — robust, Satorra–Bentler</option><option value="MLMV">MLMV — robust, mean- and variance-adjusted</option><option value="MLR">MLR — robust, Huber–White / Yuan–Bentler</option><option value="WLS">WLS — distribution-free (ADF / AGLS)</option><option value="GLS">GLS — generalised least squares</option><option value="WLSMV">WLSMV — robust weighted least squares (ordinal)</option><option value="RML">RML — robust ML, case-weighted (rsem)</option><option value="ULS">ULS — unweighted least squares</option><option value="2SLS">2SLS — MIIV two-stage least squares</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Bollen’s model-implied instrumental variables: each equation estimated separately by 2SLS, robust to misspecification in other equations, with a Sargan test per equation. Variances and covariances are estimated afterwards with the coefficients held fixed (as MIIVsem’s var.cov), which gives standardised values; there is no global fit test.</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label for="cb-parameterization">Ordinal indicators: parameterisation</label><select id="cb-parameterization" class="select"><option value="delta">Delta (default): scale factors</option><option value="theta">Theta: residual variances</option></select><div class="hint">How the latent response behind each ordinal indicator is scaled. Delta fixes its total variance at 1; theta fixes its residual variance at 1, so residual variances can be held or freed (right-click an indicator), as in Mplus PARAMETERIZATION = THETA. The fit is the same; the scale of the estimates differs.</div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Missing values</label><select class="select" aria-label="Missing values"><option value="mean">Mean replacement</option><option value="casewise">Casewise (listwise) deletion</option><option value="fiml">FIML (full-information maximum likelihood)</option><option value="twostage">Two-stage (Savalei &amp; Bentler)</option><option value="robusttwostage">Robust two-stage</option><option value="pairwise">Pairwise deletion</option><option value="mi">Multiple imputation</option></select></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Two-tailed</button><button class="" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">Percentile</button><button class="on" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button></div></div><div class="hint">BCa intervals (bias-corrected and accelerated; the jackknife adds one refit per observation); p-values from two-tailed t tests. CB-SEM bootstraps standardised paths and indirect effects.</div></div></div></aside>"
`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, cbsem mi amelia 1`] = `
"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" is a composite: in CB-SEM composites cannot be higher-order constructs or their components.</span></div><div class="issue warning clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" has two indicators; it is only identified through its relations with other factors.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" has pre-defined weights, a PLS-SEM option: switch to PLS-SEM, or estimate its weights.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>No correlation is drawn between Gamma ↔ Lambda: as exogenous constructs they are estimated as uncorrelated. Intended?</span><span class="issue-actions"><button class="btn sm">Correlate them</button><button class="btn sm ghost">Keep uncorrelated</button></span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>a3 is ordinal: choose the WLSMV estimator (thresholds and polychoric correlations), or treat it as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Multiple imputation is available for continuous indicators: no clusters, sampling weights, ordinal indicators or ESEM blocks.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Delta is marked categorical, which PLS-SEM and CPA use; CB-SEM treats it as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Alpha and Epsilon are fixed as uncorrelated, which applies to two exogenous constructs only. Delete the fixed zero.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Groups</div><select class="select"><option value="">One group (no grouping)</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">A grouping column is a numeric column with 2 to 20 values that is not an indicator (e.g. 1 = control, 2 = treatment).</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Clusters (two-level)</div><select class="select"><option value="">No clustering (one level)</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling weights</div><select class="select"><option value="">No weights</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling clusters</div><select class="select" aria-label="Sampling clusters"><option value="">No clustering</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">For cases sampled in clusters (schools, firms, countries) without modelling the levels: cluster-robust standard errors, as Mplus’s TYPE = COMPLEX.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Labels, defined parameters, tests</div><div class="hint">Right-click a path, loading or covariance → Label… Parameters with the same label are equal; labels can be used below.</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label>Held and labelled variances, intercepts, thresholds</label><div class="hint">Right-click a construct, its disturbance or an indicator → Variance…, Error variance…, Intercept… or a threshold, to hold one at a value, label it, or give values per group.</div></div><div class="field"><label>Defined parameters</label><button class="btn sm">Add defined parameter</button><div class="hint">Functions of labelled parameters, e.g. an indirect effect a*b or a difference a - b, with delta-method standard errors (lavaan :=).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Wald tests</label><button class="btn sm">Add Wald test</button><div class="hint">One hypothesis per line (left == right); all lines are tested jointly (lavaan::lavTestWald).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Constraints</label><textarea class="input mono" placeholder="a > 0
a < b
rel1 == rel2" spellcheck="false" rows="2"></textarea><div class="hint">One per line (left &gt; right, left &lt; right, or left == right), on labels and defined parameters; lavaan estimates under them. A parameter on its bound has no standard error, and χ² tests that involve active bounds are not standard.</div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>Keep variances non-negative<br><span class="hint">Bounds every variance at 0 (lavaan bounds = “pos.var”): instead of a negative variance (a Heywood case) the estimate stays at 0. Consider why it would be negative first: a misspecified model or too few cases.</span></span></label></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Covariances fixed at zero</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Not drawn: in a path diagram, no arrow means zero. Exogenous constructs otherwise covary freely.</div><div class="ind"><span>Alpha ↔ Epsilon</span><span></span><button class="btn sm ghost always" title="Let them covary freely again">Free</button></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="">PLS-SEM</button><button class="on">CB-SEM</button><button class="">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Covariance-based SEM. Common factors only; first loading of each factor fixed to 1.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Calculation engine"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">R packages</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Built-in</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">lavaan (Rosseel), running in your browser (webR), including bootstrapping (bootstrapLavaan). The first calculation loads the packages; your data never leave this computer. Monte Carlo simulation also runs in R (lavaan::simulateData, cSEM, lavaan).</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="r-backend">R runs in</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="r-backend"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on" title="webR: R compiled for the browser, with pinned package versions. Nothing to install.">This browser</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Desktop R on this computer, through the PLS Studio helper: native speed, all packages. Your data stay on this computer.">Desktop R (helper)</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">webR in this tab: nothing to install. For native speed (all cores, desktop R), get the PLS Studio Helper and choose Desktop R.<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-top: 6px;"><span class="helper-downloads"><a class="btn sm primary" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-arm64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Apple Silicon)</a><a class="btn sm" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-amd64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Intel)</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Other systems</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/blob/main/helper/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guide</a></span></div></div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="parallel-workers">Parallel bootstrap and simulation</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="parallel-workers" aria-disabled="false"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Off</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">2 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">4 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">6 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">8 sessions</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">One R session: bootstrap results are exactly those of a single run of the package with your seed. Applies to cSEM and lavaan bootstraps and Monte Carlo simulation in this browser; remembered here.</div></div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this model (data embedded): exactly what the R engine runs. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Latent interactions</div><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Product indicators</button><button class="">LMS</button><button class="">QML</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Products of mean-centred indicators (Marsh, Wen &amp; Hau, 2004), estimated by lavaan with the usual fit statistics.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Estimator</div><select class="select"><option value="ML">ML — maximum likelihood</option><option value="MLM">MLM — robust, Satorra–Bentler</option><option value="MLMV">MLMV — robust, mean- and variance-adjusted</option><option value="MLR">MLR — robust, Huber–White / Yuan–Bentler</option><option value="WLS">WLS — distribution-free (ADF / AGLS)</option><option value="GLS">GLS — generalised least squares</option><option value="WLSMV">WLSMV — robust weighted least squares (ordinal)</option><option value="RML">RML — robust ML, case-weighted (rsem)</option><option value="ULS">ULS — unweighted least squares</option><option value="2SLS">2SLS — MIIV two-stage least squares</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">ML estimates, observed-information sandwich standard errors and the Yuan–Bentler scaled χ² (Mplus variant).</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label for="cb-parameterization">Ordinal indicators: parameterisation</label><select id="cb-parameterization" class="select"><option value="delta">Delta (default): scale factors</option><option value="theta">Theta: residual variances</option></select><div class="hint">How the latent response behind each ordinal indicator is scaled. Delta fixes its total variance at 1; theta fixes its residual variance at 1, so residual variances can be held or freed (right-click an indicator), as in Mplus PARAMETERIZATION = THETA. The fit is the same; the scale of the estimates differs.</div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label for="cb-convention">Sample size in χ²</label><select id="cb-convention" class="select"><option value="lavaan">N (lavaan, Mplus)</option><option value="wishart">N − 1, Wishart likelihood (LISREL, EQS, Amos, the sem package)</option></select><div class="hint">Programs differ in whether χ² uses N or N − 1 and whether a covariance matrix is rescaled to its maximum-likelihood version; choose the convention of the program whose results you reproduce. Estimates of coefficients and loadings are the same; χ² and variances differ by a factor near N / (N − 1).</div></div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>CFI and TLI against uncorrelated variables<br><span class="hint">The baseline model in which every variable is uncorrelated (LISREL’s; lavaan’s when the syntax writes the covariances of exogenous variables out). By default the covariances among exogenous observed variables stay free in the baseline, as in Mplus and lavaan with fixed.x. Only matters with two or more exogenous observed variables.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Missing values</label><select class="select" aria-label="Missing values"><option value="mean">Mean replacement</option><option value="casewise">Casewise (listwise) deletion</option><option value="fiml">FIML (full-information maximum likelihood)</option><option value="twostage">Two-stage (Savalei &amp; Bentler)</option><option value="robusttwostage">Robust two-stage</option><option value="pairwise">Pairwise deletion</option><option value="mi">Multiple imputation</option></select><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label>Imputed data sets</label><input class="input num" min="2" max="200" type="number" value="20"><label for="mi-method" style="margin-top: 8px;">Imputation</label><select id="mi-method" class="select"><option value="mice">mice: chained equations, predictive mean matching</option><option value="micenorm">mice: Bayesian normal regression (chained equations)</option><option value="joint">Joint H1 imputation: multivariate normal data augmentation (as Mplus)</option><option value="amelia">Amelia: EM with bootstrapping (multivariate normal)</option></select><div class="field"><label>Auxiliary variables (inform the imputation, not in the model)</label><div class="pick-list"><span class="chip accent pick">1. e1<button aria-label="Remove e1"><svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"></path></svg></button></span></div><div class="pick-source"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Nominal (unordered categories; Amelia’s noms)</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" checked=""> <span>e1</span></label></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">Amelia imputes the missing values 20 times (EM with bootstrapping, multivariate normal, missing at random; seed as for bootstrapping; with e1); the model is estimated in every imputed data set and pooled by Rubin’s rules (lavaan.mi), with pooled standard errors, tests and fit.</div></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">Two-tailed</button><button class="on" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Percentile</button><button class="" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button></div></div><div class="hint">Percentile intervals; p-values from one-tailed t tests. CB-SEM bootstraps standardised paths and indirect effects.</div></div></div></aside>"
`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, cbsem wlsmv twostage 1`] = `
"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" is a composite: in CB-SEM composites cannot be higher-order constructs or their components.</span></div><div class="issue warning clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" has two indicators; it is only identified through its relations with other factors.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" has pre-defined weights, a PLS-SEM option: switch to PLS-SEM, or estimate its weights.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>No correlation is drawn between Gamma ↔ Lambda: as exogenous constructs they are estimated as uncorrelated. Intended?</span><span class="issue-actions"><button class="btn sm">Correlate them</button><button class="btn sm ghost">Keep uncorrelated</button></span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>The two-stage approach works with the ML, MLR, GLS or ULS estimator.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>The two-stage approach is for continuous indicators; with ordinal indicators (WLSMV) lavaan already uses pairwise information.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Delta is marked categorical, which PLS-SEM and CPA use; CB-SEM treats it as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>LMS is a maximum-likelihood method: choose the ML estimator.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>LMS needs complete data here: choose casewise deletion or mean replacement.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>LMS needs raw data and a single-group model without ESEM blocks or ordinal indicators.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Alpha and Epsilon are fixed as uncorrelated, which applies to two exogenous constructs only. Delete the fixed zero.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Groups</div><select class="select"><option value="">One group (no grouping)</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">A grouping column is a numeric column with 2 to 20 values that is not an indicator (e.g. 1 = control, 2 = treatment).</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Clusters (two-level)</div><select class="select"><option value="">No clustering (one level)</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling weights</div><select class="select"><option value="">No weights</option></select></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Sampling clusters</div><select class="select" aria-label="Sampling clusters"><option value="">No clustering</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">For cases sampled in clusters (schools, firms, countries) without modelling the levels: cluster-robust standard errors, as Mplus’s TYPE = COMPLEX.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Labels, defined parameters, tests</div><div class="hint">Right-click a path, loading or covariance → Label… Parameters with the same label are equal; labels can be used below.</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label>Held and labelled variances, intercepts, thresholds</label><div class="hint">Right-click a construct, its disturbance or an indicator → Variance…, Error variance…, Intercept… or a threshold, to hold one at a value, label it, or give values per group.</div></div><div class="field"><label>Defined parameters</label><button class="btn sm">Add defined parameter</button><div class="hint">Functions of labelled parameters, e.g. an indirect effect a*b or a difference a - b, with delta-method standard errors (lavaan :=).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Wald tests</label><button class="btn sm">Add Wald test</button><div class="hint">One hypothesis per line (left == right); all lines are tested jointly (lavaan::lavTestWald).</div></div><div class="field"><label>Constraints</label><textarea class="input mono" placeholder="a > 0
a < b
rel1 == rel2" spellcheck="false" rows="2"></textarea><div class="hint">One per line (left &gt; right, left &lt; right, or left == right), on labels and defined parameters; lavaan estimates under them. A parameter on its bound has no standard error, and χ² tests that involve active bounds are not standard.</div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>Keep variances non-negative<br><span class="hint">Bounds every variance at 0 (lavaan bounds = “pos.var”): instead of a negative variance (a Heywood case) the estimate stays at 0. Consider why it would be negative first: a misspecified model or too few cases.</span></span></label></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Covariances fixed at zero</div><div class="hint" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Not drawn: in a path diagram, no arrow means zero. Exogenous constructs otherwise covary freely.</div><div class="ind"><span>Alpha ↔ Epsilon</span><span></span><button class="btn sm ghost always" title="Let them covary freely again">Free</button></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="">PLS-SEM</button><button class="on">CB-SEM</button><button class="">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Covariance-based SEM. Common factors only; first loading of each factor fixed to 1.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Calculation engine"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">R packages</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Built-in</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">lavaan (Rosseel), running in your browser (webR), including bootstrapping (bootstrapLavaan). The first calculation loads the packages; your data never leave this computer. Monte Carlo simulation also runs in R (lavaan::simulateData, cSEM, lavaan).</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="r-backend">R runs in</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="r-backend"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on" title="webR: R compiled for the browser, with pinned package versions. Nothing to install.">This browser</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Desktop R on this computer, through the PLS Studio helper: native speed, all packages. Your data stay on this computer.">Desktop R (helper)</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">webR in this tab: nothing to install. For native speed (all cores, desktop R), get the PLS Studio Helper and choose Desktop R.<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-top: 6px;"><span class="helper-downloads"><a class="btn sm primary" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-arm64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Apple Silicon)</a><a class="btn sm" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-amd64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Intel)</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Other systems</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/blob/main/helper/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guide</a></span></div></div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="parallel-workers">Parallel bootstrap and simulation</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="parallel-workers" aria-disabled="false"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Off</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">2 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">4 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">6 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">8 sessions</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">One R session: bootstrap results are exactly those of a single run of the package with your seed. Applies to cSEM and lavaan bootstraps and Monte Carlo simulation in this browser; remembered here.</div></div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this model (data embedded): exactly what the R engine runs. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Latent interactions</div><div class="segmented"><button class="">Product indicators</button><button class="on">LMS</button><button class="">QML</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Latent moderated structural equations (Klein &amp; Moosbrugger, 2000; modsem): maximum likelihood for the latent product itself, without product indicators; usually the most efficient. Fit statistics are for the model without the interaction. Bootstrap: cases are resampled and the model refitted with modsem, which is slow (LMS: seconds per sample); try 200 samples first.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Estimator</div><select class="select"><option value="ML">ML — maximum likelihood</option><option value="MLM">MLM — robust, Satorra–Bentler</option><option value="MLMV">MLMV — robust, mean- and variance-adjusted</option><option value="MLR">MLR — robust, Huber–White / Yuan–Bentler</option><option value="WLS">WLS — distribution-free (ADF / AGLS)</option><option value="GLS">GLS — generalised least squares</option><option value="WLSMV">WLSMV — robust weighted least squares (ordinal)</option><option value="RML">RML — robust ML, case-weighted (rsem)</option><option value="ULS">ULS — unweighted least squares</option><option value="2SLS">2SLS — MIIV two-stage least squares</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Diagonally weighted least squares on polychoric correlations, with robust standard errors and a mean- and variance-adjusted χ² (Muthén; lavaan). The estimator for ordinal indicators (mark them with right-click → Treat as ordinal). Needs the R engine.</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label for="cb-parameterization">Ordinal indicators: parameterisation</label><select id="cb-parameterization" class="select"><option value="delta">Delta (default): scale factors</option><option value="theta">Theta: residual variances</option></select><div class="hint">How the latent response behind each ordinal indicator is scaled. Delta fixes its total variance at 1; theta fixes its residual variance at 1, so residual variances can be held or freed (right-click an indicator), as in Mplus PARAMETERIZATION = THETA. The fit is the same; the scale of the estimates differs.</div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label for="cb-wlsmv-se">Standard errors</label><select id="cb-wlsmv-se" class="select"><option value="mplus">Mplus / classic WLSMV (default)</option><option value="lavaan">lavaan 0.7 (observed information in the sandwich)</option></select><div class="hint">As Mplus and lavaan up to 0.7-1 (Muthén, du Toit &amp; Spisic 1997): the expected information (Δ′WΔ)⁻¹ in the sandwich (information.bread = “expected”) and the covariance matrix of the estimates divided by N. Estimates and the test statistic do not change. With sampling clusters or weights lavaan’s own standard errors are kept.</div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>Test statistic as Mplus<br><span class="hint">lavaan’s mimic = “Mplus” (with gamma.vcov.mplus = FALSE): the mean- and variance-adjusted χ² Mplus prints, and Mplus’s handling of covariates with mixed continuous and ordinal outcomes; estimates can move in the third decimal. With groups the options mimic sets for the test statistic are written out (mimic itself would also hold loadings and thresholds equal in a configural model), so the groups’ equalities stay those chosen here.</span></span></label></div><label class="check" style="margin-top: 8px;"><input type="checkbox"><span>CFI and TLI against uncorrelated variables<br><span class="hint">The baseline model in which every variable is uncorrelated (LISREL’s; lavaan’s when the syntax writes the covariances of exogenous variables out). By default the covariances among exogenous observed variables stay free in the baseline, as in Mplus and lavaan with fixed.x. Only matters with two or more exogenous observed variables.</span></span></label></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Missing values</label><select class="select" aria-label="Missing values"><option value="mean">Mean replacement</option><option value="casewise">Casewise (listwise) deletion</option><option value="fiml">FIML (full-information maximum likelihood)</option><option value="twostage">Two-stage (Savalei &amp; Bentler)</option><option value="robusttwostage">Robust two-stage</option><option value="pairwise">Pairwise deletion</option><option value="mi">Multiple imputation</option></select><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">Two-stage (Savalei &amp; Bentler 2009; lavaan missing = "two.stage"): the saturated means and covariances are estimated from all observed values (EM), then the model is fitted to them, with standard errors and a χ² corrected for the first stage. ML, MLR, GLS or ULS.</div><div style="margin-top: 8px;"><div class="field"><label>Auxiliary variables (inform the missing values, not in the model)</label><div class="pick-list"><span class="hint">Click columns below to add them.</span></div><div class="pick-source"></div></div><div class="hint">lavaan’s aux =: with FIML each auxiliary variable is correlated with every observed variable of the model and with the others (saturated correlates, Graham 2003), which makes missing at random more plausible without changing the model or its degrees of freedom; with the two-stage approach they join the first-stage EM. Continuous columns; no ordinal indicators or clusters.</div></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Two-tailed</button><button class="" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Percentile</button><button class="" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button></div></div><div class="hint">Percentile intervals; p-values from two-tailed t tests. CB-SEM bootstraps standardised paths and indirect effects.</div></div></div></aside>"
`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, pls 1`] = `"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Epsilon" is not connected to any other construct.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": an estimated first component loading is a CB-SEM option.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": component loadings are held at values in CB-SEM only.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Alpha" is a component of "Gamma" and cannot also be in the structural model (cSEM’s two-stage approach); connect "Gamma" instead.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" is a component of "Gamma" and cannot also be in the structural model (cSEM’s two-stage approach); connect "Gamma" instead.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a1" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a2" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" is not connected to any other construct.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Delta" is categorical: it can only predict (an exogenous variable), not be predicted.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>PLS-SEM treats the ordinal indicators (a3) as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>The model has 1 correlation (double-headed arrows); PLS-SEM ignores them. They are estimated in CB-SEM.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="on">PLS-SEM</button><button class="">CB-SEM</button><button class="">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Variance-based: common factors and composites. Turn on PLSc for consistent estimates of common-factor models.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Second-order constructs</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Second-order approach"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Two-stage</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Embedded two-stage</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Repeated indicators</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">Disjoint two-stage (Sarstedt et al., 2019): the first-order constructs are estimated without the second-order construct; their scores are then its indicators. cSEM’s .approach_2ndorder = "2stage", seminr’s two_stage.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Calculation engine"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">R packages</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Built-in</button></div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="PLS package" style="margin-top: 8px;"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">cSEM</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">seminr</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="cSEM's .approach_weights: PLS path modeling uses each construct's own mode (Inspector, Outer weights); the others weight every construct the same way">Weighting approach (all constructs, cSEM)</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Weighting approach (all constructs, cSEM)" style="margin-top: 4px;"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on" title="Partial least squares path modeling">PLS-PM</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Generalized structured component analysis (Hwang &amp; Takane 2004): weights from one global least-squares criterion; with PLSc on, GSCAm for common factors">GSCA</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Principal component analysis: each construct is the first principal component of its indicators">PCA</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Sum-score regression: each construct is the (standardised) sum of its indicators, then regressions among them">Sum scores</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">cSEM (Rademaker &amp; Schuberth), running in your browser (webR): PLS, PLSc, composites, bootstrapping, the model fit test and IPMA. Interactions use cSEM’s products of construct scores. The first calculation loads the packages; your data never leave this computer. Monte Carlo simulation also runs in R (lavaan::simulateData, cSEM, lavaan).</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="r-backend">R runs in</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="r-backend"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on" title="webR: R compiled for the browser, with pinned package versions. Nothing to install.">This browser</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Desktop R on this computer, through the PLS Studio helper: native speed, all packages. Your data stay on this computer.">Desktop R (helper)</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">webR in this tab: nothing to install. For native speed (all cores, desktop R), get the PLS Studio Helper and choose Desktop R.<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-top: 6px;"><span class="helper-downloads"><a class="btn sm primary" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-arm64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Apple Silicon)</a><a class="btn sm" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-amd64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Intel)</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Other systems</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/blob/main/helper/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guide</a></span></div></div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="parallel-workers">Parallel bootstrap and simulation</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="parallel-workers" aria-disabled="false"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Off</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">2 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">4 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">6 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">8 sessions</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">One R session: bootstrap results are exactly those of a single run of the package with your seed. Applies to cSEM and lavaan bootstraps and Monte Carlo simulation in this browser; remembered here.</div></div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this model (data embedded): exactly what the R engine runs. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">PLS algorithm</div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Consistent PLS (PLSc)</b><br><span class="hint">Corrects common factors for attenuation using ρA (Dijkstra &amp; Henseler, 2015).</span></span></label><div class="field"><label>Inner weighting scheme</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Path</button><button class="">Factor</button><button class="">Centroid</button></div></div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Max iterations</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="10000" step="1" type="number" value="300"></div><div class="field"><label>Stop criterion 10^−x</label><input class="input num" min="3" max="12" step="1" type="number" value="7"></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Missing values</label><select class="select" aria-label="Missing values"><option value="mean">Mean replacement</option><option value="casewise">Casewise (listwise) deletion</option><option value="mi">Multiple imputation (mice)</option></select></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Two-tailed</button><button class="" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Percentile</button><button class="" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button><button class="" title="Bootstrap-t (Efron &amp; Tibshirani 1993): each subsample gets its own standard error from an inner bootstrap. Accurate, slow; runs in the built-in engine">Studentized</button></div></div><div class="hint">Percentile intervals; p-values from two-tailed t tests. The same subsample count is used for the fit test (HI95/HI99).</div></div></div></aside>"`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, pls cSEM gsca builtin 1`] = `"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Epsilon" is not connected to any other construct.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma" is a second-order construct: in PLS these are estimated by cSEM or seminr. Choose “R packages” under Calculated by.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": an estimated first component loading is a CB-SEM option.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": component loadings are held at values in CB-SEM only.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Alpha" is a component of "Gamma" and cannot also be in the structural model (cSEM’s two-stage approach); connect "Gamma" instead.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" is a component of "Gamma" and cannot also be in the structural model (cSEM’s two-stage approach); connect "Gamma" instead.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a1" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a2" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" is not connected to any other construct.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>The GSCA weighting approach is estimated with cSEM: choose “R packages” under Calculated by.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Delta" is categorical: it can only predict (an exogenous variable), not be predicted.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>PLS-SEM treats the ordinal indicators (a3) as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue error"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>GSCA is estimated with cSEM: choose R packages → cSEM, or PLS path modeling.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>The model has 1 correlation (double-headed arrows); PLS-SEM ignores them. They are estimated in CB-SEM.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="on">PLS-SEM</button><button class="">CB-SEM</button><button class="">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Variance-based: common factors and composites. Turn on PLSc for consistent estimates of common-factor models.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Second-order constructs</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Second-order approach"><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Two-stage</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Embedded two-stage</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Repeated indicators</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">Embedded two-stage (Ringle, Sarstedt &amp; Straub, 2012): the first stage uses the repeated indicators, so the second-order construct is in the model from the start; its dimensions’ scores are then its indicators. cSEM’s .approach_2ndorder = "mixed"; not in seminr.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Calculation engine"><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">R packages</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Built-in</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">PLS Studio’s own implementation, validated against the R packages. Instant, no download.</div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this model (data embedded): exactly what the R engine runs. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">PLS algorithm</div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox"><span><b>Consistent PLS (PLSc)</b><br><span class="hint">Corrects common factors for attenuation using ρA (Dijkstra &amp; Henseler, 2015).</span></span></label><div class="field"><label>Inner weighting scheme</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Path</button><button class="">Factor</button><button class="">Centroid</button></div></div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Max iterations</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="10000" step="1" type="number" value="300"></div><div class="field"><label>Stop criterion 10^−x</label><input class="input num" min="3" max="12" step="1" type="number" value="7"></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Missing values</label><select class="select" aria-label="Missing values"><option value="mean">Mean replacement</option><option value="casewise">Casewise (listwise) deletion</option><option value="mi">Multiple imputation (mice)</option></select></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Two-tailed</button><button class="" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Percentile</button><button class="" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button><button class="" title="Bootstrap-t (Efron &amp; Tibshirani 1993): each subsample gets its own standard error from an inner bootstrap. Accurate, slow; runs in the built-in engine">Studentized</button></div></div><div class="hint">Percentile intervals; p-values from two-tailed t tests. The same subsample count is used for the fit test (HI95/HI99).</div></div></div></aside>"`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, pls seminr mi 1`] = `"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Epsilon" is not connected to any other construct.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma" is a second-order construct: with consistent PLS these are estimated by cSEM. Choose cSEM, or turn off PLSc for seminr.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": an estimated first component loading is a CB-SEM option.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": component loadings are held at values in CB-SEM only.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Alpha" is a component of "Gamma" and cannot also be in the structural model (cSEM’s two-stage approach); connect "Gamma" instead.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" is a component of "Gamma" and cannot also be in the structural model (cSEM’s two-stage approach); connect "Gamma" instead.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a1" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a2" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" is not connected to any other construct.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Moderation (Beta moderating Alpha → Delta) with PLSc needs cSEM or the built-in engine: choose one of those, or switch consistent PLS off.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Delta" is categorical: it can only predict (an exogenous variable), not be predicted.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>seminr has no dominant indicators: the signs of Alpha are as estimated. Choose cSEM to fix them.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>PLS-SEM treats the ordinal indicators (a3) as continuous.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>The model has 1 correlation (double-headed arrows); PLS-SEM ignores them. They are estimated in CB-SEM.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="on">PLS-SEM</button><button class="">CB-SEM</button><button class="">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Variance-based: common factors and composites. Turn on PLSc for consistent estimates of common-factor models.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Second-order constructs</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Second-order approach"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Two-stage</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Embedded two-stage</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Repeated indicators</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">Disjoint two-stage (Sarstedt et al., 2019): the first-order constructs are estimated without the second-order construct; their scores are then its indicators. cSEM’s .approach_2ndorder = "2stage", seminr’s two_stage.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Calculation engine"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">R packages</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">Built-in</button></div><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="PLS package" style="margin-top: 8px;"><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">cSEM</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">seminr</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">seminr (Ray, Danks &amp; Calero Valdez), running in your browser (webR): PLS, PLSc for reflective constructs, two-stage interactions. No model-fit statistics; path and factor schemes only. seminr’s bootstrap needs worker processes, so bootstrap with cSEM here (or export the script). The fit test and IPMA use cSEM. The first calculation loads the packages; your data never leave this computer. Monte Carlo simulation also runs in R (lavaan::simulateData, cSEM, lavaan).</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="r-backend">R runs in</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="r-backend"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on" title="webR: R compiled for the browser, with pinned package versions. Nothing to install.">This browser</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="" title="Desktop R on this computer, through the PLS Studio helper: native speed, all packages. Your data stay on this computer.">Desktop R (helper)</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">webR in this tab: nothing to install. For native speed (all cores, desktop R), get the PLS Studio Helper and choose Desktop R.<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-top: 6px;"><span class="helper-downloads"><a class="btn sm primary" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-arm64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Apple Silicon)</a><a class="btn sm" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest/download/PLS-Studio-Helper-amd64.dmg" rel="noreferrer">Download for macOS (Intel)</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Other systems</a><a class="btn sm ghost" href="https://github.com/stolucc/pls-studio/blob/main/helper/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guide</a></span></div></div></div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label id="parallel-workers">Parallel bootstrap and simulation</label><div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="parallel-workers" aria-disabled="false"><button role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="on">Off</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">2 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">4 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">6 sessions</button><button role="radio" aria-checked="false" class="">8 sessions</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">One R session: bootstrap results are exactly those of a single run of the package with your seed. Applies to cSEM and lavaan bootstraps and Monte Carlo simulation in this browser; remembered here.</div></div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this model (data embedded): exactly what the R engine runs. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">PLS algorithm</div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" checked=""><span><b>Consistent PLS (PLSc)</b><br><span class="hint">Corrects common factors for attenuation using ρA (Dijkstra &amp; Henseler, 2015).</span></span></label><div class="field"><label>Inner weighting scheme</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Path</button><button class="">Factor</button><button class="">Centroid</button></div></div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Max iterations</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="10000" step="1" type="number" value="300"></div><div class="field"><label>Stop criterion 10^−x</label><input class="input num" min="3" max="12" step="1" type="number" value="7"></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Missing values</label><select class="select" aria-label="Missing values"><option value="mean">Mean replacement</option><option value="casewise">Casewise (listwise) deletion</option><option value="mi">Multiple imputation (mice)</option></select><div class="field" style="margin-top: 8px;"><label>Imputed data sets</label><input class="input num" min="2" max="200" type="number" value="20"><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 6px;">mice imputes the missing values 20 times (predictive mean matching, missing at random; seed as for bootstrapping); the model is estimated in every imputed data set and the estimates are averaged; bootstrapping pools the bootstrap standard errors by Rubin’s rules.</div></div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Two-tailed</button><button class="" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">Percentile</button><button class="" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button><button class="on" title="Bootstrap-t (Efron &amp; Tibshirani 1993): each subsample gets its own standard error from an inner bootstrap. Accurate, slow; runs in the built-in engine">Studentized</button></div></div><div class="hint">Studentized intervals (bootstrap-t; 50 inner samples per subsample, so about 51 times as long; built-in engine); p-values from two-tailed t tests. The same subsample count is used for the fit test (HI95/HI99).</div></div></div></aside>"`;

exports[`Inspector markup > model, process 1`] = `"<aside class="panel right" aria-label="Inspector"><div class="panel-head"><span>Model</span></div><div class="panel-body"><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Checks</div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": an estimated first component loading is a CB-SEM option.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma": component loadings are held at values in CB-SEM only.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Gamma" is a higher-order construct; these are supported in CB-SEM only.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a1" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "a2" is assigned to both "Alpha" and "Lambda".</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Beta" has pre-defined weights, a PLS-SEM option: switch to PLS-SEM, or estimate its weights.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>Indicator "d1" (in "Delta") is constant (0 in every row): it carries no information.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>A conditional process model has one antecedent X, but Alpha, Gamma have no incoming paths. Make the others mediators or moderators, or mark them as covariates.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" is not in the model: connect it, use it as a moderator, or mark it as a covariate.</span></div><div class="issue warning clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Lambda" is a latent variable with two items; it is identified only through its relations with other latent variables.</span></div><div class="issue error clickable"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>"Delta" is marked as categorical, which applies to X only.</span></div><div class="issue warning"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 8v5M12 16h.01"></path></svg> <span>The model has 1 correlation (double-headed arrows); regression ignores them. They are estimated in CB-SEM.</span></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Method</div><div class="segmented"><button class="">PLS-SEM</button><button class="">CB-SEM</button><button class="on">CPA</button></div><div class="hint" style="margin-top: 8px;">Conditional process analysis (Hayes): mediation, moderation and moderated mediation with observed variables or scale means, one OLS regression per outcome, bootstrap confidence intervals for indirect effects.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Calculated by</div><div class="hint">manymome (Cheung &amp; Cheung, 2024), running in your browser (webR): OLS regressions (lm), the percentile bootstrap of indirect effects and conditional effects at moderator values. Every numbered model was checked against PROCESS for R on the same data. Your data never leave this computer.</div><button class="btn sm" style="margin-top: 8px;" title="Download the R script for this analysis (data embedded): exactly what runs here. Open it in R or RStudio to reproduce the results.">Export R script</button></div><div class="section"><div class="field"><label>Probe moderators at</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">16th / 50th / 84th pct.</button><button class="on">Mean ± 1 SD</button></div></div><div class="hint">Percentiles are PROCESS’s default. A moderator with two values is probed at both. Missing values: listwise deletion, as PROCESS.</div><div class="field" style="margin-top: 10px;"><label>Standard errors of the regressions</label><select class="select"><option value="none">OLS (assumes constant error variance)</option><option value="HC0">HC0 (White)</option><option value="HC1">HC1</option><option value="HC2">HC2</option><option value="HC3">HC3 (recommended; Long &amp; Ervin, 2000)</option><option value="HC4">HC4 (Cribari-Neto)</option></select></div><div class="hint">Heteroskedasticity-consistent standard errors (PROCESS’s hc option) for coefficients, conditional effects, F tests and Johnson–Neyman; bootstrap intervals of indirect effects do not use them. Latent-variable models use SAM’s standard errors instead.</div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-title">Bootstrapping</div><div class="row2"><div class="field"><label>Subsamples</label><input class="input num" min="10" max="100000" step="100" type="number" value="1000"></div><div class="field"><label>Random seed</label><input class="input num" min="0" max="2147483648" step="1" type="number" value="1234"></div></div><div class="field"><label>Confidence interval</label><div class="segmented"><button class="">90%</button><button class="on">95%</button><button class="">99%</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Tests</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Two-tailed</button><button class="" title="For directional hypotheses: p for the direction of the estimate (half the two-tailed p), intervals from α to 1 − α">One-tailed</button></div></div><div class="field"><label>Intervals</label><div class="segmented"><button class="on">Percentile</button><button class="" title="Bias-corrected and accelerated (Efron 1987): adds a jackknife, one refit per observation">BCa</button></div></div><div class="hint">Percentile intervals; p-values from two-tailed t tests. Indirect effects and indices of moderated mediation; direct and conditional effects use OLS standard errors, as PROCESS. At least 100 samples (5000 recommended for reporting).</div></div></div></aside>"`;
